{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1534099-weapons-and-armor-feel-completely-unbalanced","id":1534099,"title":"Weapons and Armor Feel Completely Unbalanced","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-12T10:26:51-07:00","id":1534099,"title":"Weapons and Armor Feel Completely Unbalanced","content":"I'll be running a Changeling: The Dreaming game soon, and going through the equipment section feels like it was written without any balance in mind. Lets start with Shields.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Shields</b>: Shields are large items the wielder interposes between attacks and his body. Shields increase the difficulty of attacking the wielder in close combat by +1 or +2, depending upon the size of the shield \u2014 the attacker needs to work to avoid hitting the shield rather than his target. The wielder can also use a shield to parry both close combat and ranged attacks. Rolls to use a shield to parry ranged attacks with arrows or thrown weapons are made versus difficulty 6 (rather than the normal difficulty 8 for parrying ranged attacks). In addition, if the wielder makes a successful parry roll (also versus difficulty 6), she can use the shield\u2019s armor (see Shields, p. 285) against attacks by firearms. Using a shield to parry or provide armor against an attack requires a successful parry maneuver, but when used to provide armor against a firearms attack, the parry roll isn\u2019t resisted \u2014 the character just attempts to place the shield between her and the bullets.&quot;<br /> <br /> So Shields give the opponent a passive difficulty increase of +2 for a regular shield. So far so good. However, you can also use the Parry Maneuver with it against both Close Combat and Ranged Attacks. Using Parry against Firearms seems to have it's own special rule, where you don't contest it, but instead roll Melee + Parry at Difficulty 6 and all you need is 1 Success to get to add your armor to your Soak. Easy to understand and seems fair. You also have an easier time Parrying Bows, Crossbows and Thrown attacks with a shield. Again understandable.<br /> <br /> It's when you get to the Parry Maneuver versus Close Combat that it starts to feel a bit wacky. I'm not quite sure how people are supposed to actually fight each other when they each have shields. Not only are you at a +2 Difficulty to hit them, which is already a huge disadvantage in combat, but it seems that Shields can use the Parry Maneuver as normal, with no downsides, while fighting in Close Combat. A Wooden Shield in particular only gives you a -1 Dexterity Penalty, which is negligible compared to the passive +2 Difficulty you're imposing. Getting both the Passive and Active defense with a very minimal penalty feels wrong, and two people both fighting each other with shields feels like it would last forever, especially if you combine it with armor. And fighting with a big two handed weapon, doesn't seem like it would make up for the increased Difficulty. Even a Great Sword (Which I go into detail below), by far the best two handed weapon, turns into a Difficulty 7 to Hit, that can still be parried at Difficulty 6. And while it hits hard at Str +6/L Damage, if the opponent has Fae Mail, they're still getting +3 to their Soak. All of that is before the fact that increasing someone's Difficulty also increases their chance to Botch, swinging it in favor of always using a Shield even further.<br /> <br /> As for weapons: A Short Sword is Difficulty 5 to use, with Str +2/L damage. A Sword is Difficulty 6 to use, with Str +2/L damage. A Broadsword is Difficulty 6 to use with Str +3/L damage. Why does a Sword even exist? A Short Sword has the same damage and is easier to use, and a Broad Sword is the same difficulty to use, but does more damage. A Great Axe and Great Sword are both Str +6/L that can't be concealed and require two hands to use. But the Great Axe is Difficulty 7 and the Great Sword is Difficulty 5? And poor Huge Spiked Club is ALSO Difficulty 7, non-concealable and requires two hands...but is only Str +4/L. Other than if you REALLY wanted to roleplay having those specific weapons, the Great Sword outperforms both of the other weapons my miles due to the -2 Difficulty (And +2 damage over the Huge Spiked Club).<br /> <br /> The balance of equipment just seems all over the place, often copy/pasted from other World of Darkness gamelines, without much thought on how these will interact in a game that is much more focused around the fact that people will likely be using more weapons and armor, due to the more medieval vibe the game gives off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T11:15:28-07:00","id":1534100,"title":"","content":"Equipment is meant to give you an advantage, if it wasn't better than not using it, no one would use it. But yes, swords are generally better than other weapons in roleplaying games simply because swords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T11:51:33-07:00","id":1534101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1534099-weapons-and-armor-feel-completely-unbalanced?p=1534100#post1534100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Equipment is meant to give you an advantage, if it wasn't better than not using it, no one would use it. But yes, swords are generally better than other weapons in roleplaying games simply because swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is about HOW much better it is. Using a Shield is almost always better than using a two handed weapon, and not by a small margin. You could use your own argument about Two Handed weapons and how THEY aren't worth using when Shields exist. So using your logic, why do Two Handed Weapons exist, when it's worse than using a Shield?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T13:11:29-07:00","id":1534104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1534099-weapons-and-armor-feel-completely-unbalanced?p=1534101#post1534101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is about HOW much better it is. Using a Shield is almost always better than using a two handed weapon, and not by a small margin. You could use your own argument about Two Handed weapons and how THEY aren't worth using when Shields exist. So using your logic, why do Two Handed Weapons exist, when it's worse than using a Shield?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You didn't compare apples to apples. First, you put the shield in a situation where the shield is at it's worst and the 2 handed user in the situation that is it's worst. Even then you didn't do the math. From the numbers you gave, let's assume person A has a shield and sword and person B has a 2 handed sword. The two handed sword loses 2 successes on a dice pool of 10 dice, but gains 3 damage over the shield user. That's a fairly significant advantage to the 2 handed weapon user. <br /> <br /> Second, you just decided &quot;and they parry&quot; without accounting for parrying taking their turn. I guarantee you in a combat where one person does nothing but defend and another person does nothing but attack, eventually the attacker will get lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T14:30:00-07:00","id":1534107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1534099-weapons-and-armor-feel-completely-unbalanced?p=1534104#post1534104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. You didn't compare apples to apples. First, you put the shield in a situation where the shield is at it's worst and the 2 handed user in the situation that is it's worst. Even then you didn't do the math. From the numbers you gave, let's assume person A has a shield and sword and person B has a 2 handed sword. The two handed sword loses 2 successes on a dice pool of 10 dice, but gains 3 damage over the shield user. That's a fairly significant advantage to the 2 handed weapon user.<br /> <br /> Second, you just decided &quot;and they parry&quot; without accounting for parrying taking their turn. I guarantee you in a combat where one person does nothing but defend and another person does nothing but attack, eventually the attacker will get lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be forgetting that you can split Actions? It doesn't sound like you're taking that into account. Remember, if the Great Sword gets parried it does 0 Damage. So lets do the math, as you suggest. Now mind you, we're using the Great Sword, which is by far the best two handed weapon. I'm giving you the advantage in this argument because if we use the Great Axe, Polearm, or Huge Spiked Club it's not even a contest as they start hitting on 9's.<br /> <br /> Since you used 10 dice as an example, I'll do the same. The two combatants are both master swordsmen. They both obviously want to attack and defend, so they'll be splitting their Actions between both. Combatant A has the Great Sword, Combatant B has the Broadsword and Shield.<br /> <br /> Combatant A tries splitting evenly. 5 to attack, 5 to parry. This gives him roughly a 50/50 (Not quite due to 1's taking away and potential specialties but for the moment we'll just call it 50%) to defend, but only about a 40% to hit. So 2 on the hit, and 2.5 on the Parry.<br /> <br /> Combatant B doesn't need to split evenly, but lets say he does. He has a 50/50 on both attack AND defense. He'll be getting 2.5 successes to defend, and 2.5 to attack. Do you now see why it's problematic? I'll reiterate, if the Great Sword gets parried, it doesn't matter how much damage potential it has. It could do Str +10/L and it wouldn't matter, because if it's parried it does 0 and parrying becomes MUCH more reliable and easy when the person is hitting on 7's. The odds will be in Combatant B's favor, the entire time. And that's using a weapon that I would call OP, because it has a lower difficulty and higher damage than almost every other weapon in the book. That's giving you the best possible scenario, using an overpowered weapon option.<br /> <br /> What if a player wasn't meta-gaming and REALLY liked two handed axes or huge spiked clubs? Well THAT person is hitting a Shield on a 9's. Even if the Great Axe person uses all 10 dice to hit, he's getting on average 2 successes. The Shield user could put 8 dice to defense and 2 to attack the entire time and just slowly wittle them down while the Great Axe user has basically a 0% to hit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T14:46:16-07:00","id":1534108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1534099-weapons-and-armor-feel-completely-unbalanced?p=1534107#post1534107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be forgetting that you can split Actions? It doesn't sound like you're taking that into account. Remember, if the Great Sword gets parried it does 0 Damage. So lets do the math, as you suggest. Now mind you, we're using the Great Sword, which is by far the best two handed weapon. I'm giving you the advantage in this argument because if we use the Great Axe, Polearm, or Huge Spiked Club it's not even a contest as they start hitting on 9's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already conceded the great sword was better than other 2 handed weapons &quot;because sword&quot; you don't need to harp on it, nor are you &quot;giving me an advantage&quot;, if you want to prove an option is over powered, you don't prove it by comparing it to the worst option available, you compare them to other good options.<br /> <br /> But I will admit to being rusty with combat rules, I'm more a chronicles person. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since you used 10 dice as an example, I'll do the same. The two combatants are both master swordsmen. They both obviously want to attack and defend, so they'll be splitting their Actions between both. Combatant A has the Great Sword, Combatant B has the Broadsword and Shield.<br /> <br /> Combatant A tries splitting evenly. 5 to attack, 5 to parry. This gives him roughly a 50/50 (Not quite due to 1's taking away and potential specialties but for the moment we'll just call it 50%) to defend, but only about a 40% to hit. So 2 on the hit, and 2.5 on the Parry.<br /> <br /> Combatant B doesn't need to split evenly, but lets say he does. He has a 50/50 on both attack AND defense. He'll be getting 2.5 successes to defend, and 2.5 to attack. Do you now see why it's problematic? I'll reiterate, if the Great Sword gets parried, it doesn't matter how much damage potential it has. It could do Str +10/L and it wouldn't matter, because if it's parried it does 0 and parrying becomes MUCH more reliable and easy when the person is hitting on 7's. The odds will be in Combatant B's favor, the entire time. And that's using a weapon that I would call OP, because it has a lower difficulty and higher damage than almost every other weapon in the book. That's giving you the best possible scenario, using an overpowered weapon option. </div> </div> </div>No, they don't both want to attack and defend. You don't wield a great sword to defend, you wield a great sword to attack and end combat quickly. So let's pretend the person with the great sword isn't an idiot and decided to put all their dice towards the attack.They blow through the block, deal a massive wound to the shield user, who now gets to attack back with wound penalties, if they're still on their feet. Assuming, of course, that they're allowed to defend at all, given that person A in your example has the initiative. <br /> <br /> I suspect that if you find a combat simulator like a hundred times or so you'll find that the differences between these two combatants aren't nearly as significant as you think and that initiative means far more for determining who wins than what they're equipped with. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T16:27:16-07:00","id":1534112,"title":"","content":"Changeling is not a system really designed around things like &quot;balance&quot;. You're pointing out &quot;failures&quot; at something that isn't a goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T18:59:13-07:00","id":1534117,"title":"","content":"Huge Spiked Clubs can be used against metal targets without suffering nearly as much damage as a greatsword blade. Basically, if you enforce a modicum of real life consequences, you can shore up some of the wild differences in weapon stats (and of course, if you get shot with a bow before you can close the distance, there's also that!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T12:06:14-07:00","id":1534141,"title":"","content":"First off: yes the weapon and armor stat blocks are wonky. You can adjust them if you'd like, but it really depends what you want if just moving some numbers around is going to change anything compared to doing a more comprehensive combat overhaul.<br /> <br /> Second: Mean average results are not destiny. If the defender as a mean parry result of 2.5 and the attack has a mean attack result of 2, that's roughly 1/4 of the time the attacker will hit. Given that CtD (and the rest of the WoD) lack resurrection, characters have small Health pools, and soak isn't that impressive for most things in the games, that one hit from a heavy weapon could be fight ending (stunning if not outright incapacitating).<br /> <br /> 75% of the time you win but will likely need weeks of recovery or healing magic before you can risk combat again, and 25% of the time your PC is dead and you have to make a new one? How many players really want to risk that?<br /> <br /> There's a massive gap between completely imbalanced weapons rules (and not even ones that make sense from some &quot;realism&quot; perspective), and rules that are so broken there is a One True Build that will let you win every fight without risk or worry and make combat meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}